<##
$$
W
  ====
  - [[Page~211 #11: 纊(3)]]
    --
    A colloquial word;
    --
    ==
    - to latch, to fasten or loop two doors, with a string or hoop;
    - _kw(a/)ng(3) (4)m(a/)i (4)m(u/)n_
        [[gwaang3 maai4 mun4]],
        fasten the door;
    - _kw(a/)ng(3) (2)kau_
        [[gwaang3 gau2]],
        to tie up a dog;
    - _yat(7) kw(a/)ng(3) lang(3)_
        [[jat1 gwaang3 lang3]]
        a number or load of things tied together.
    ==
    <# TODO: normalise below to $纊kwang3 #>
    ==
    - To rub against, to run upon one in the street;
    - _kw(a/)ng(3) (1)ts(')an (5)k(')(u:)_
        [[gwaang3 can1 keoi5]],
        rubbed against it;
    - _kw(a/)ng(3) l(a/)n(6) (1)sh(a/)m_
        [[gwaang3 laan6 saam1]],
        to tear one's dress by catching it;
    - _kw(a/)ng(3) (5)k(')(u:) lok(9) (4)lai_
        [[gwaang3 keoi5 lok6 lai4]],
        catch it (a kite) down;
    - _(2)t(')ai kw(a/)ng(3)_
        [[tai2 gwaang3]]
        lookout, [lest I] run against you!---a porter's cry.
    ==
  ====
$$
